WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:07.509
Far removed from the bright lights of normal
human civilisation, in some of the darkest

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:13.449
recesses of Earth’s great expanse, are spine
tingling and hellishly creepy places that

00:00:13.449 --> 00:00:16.259
even the most intrepid of adventurer’s daren’t
wander.

00:00:16.259 --> 00:00:25.160
Here’s the seven creepiest places on Earth.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.160
First up is Hoia Baciu forest in Romania.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.050
This place is like the Bermuda Triangle of
forests.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.640
The forest is renowned in Romania for its
spooky and paranormal happenings.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:42.180
Situated in north Romania this spooky wilderness
has been home to ghost sightings, UFO sightings,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.540
disappearances and faces appearing in photographs
that weren't there when the photo was being

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.540
taken.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.290
People who visit the forest often report an
overwhelming feeling that they are being watched.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:58.740
People who enter the forest get unexplainable
rashes and sometimes fall ill.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.930
Electronic devices often refuse to work inside
the forest.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:07.500
The locals tell stories of the first ever,
reported paranormal case in the forest.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.640
They claim a shepherd mysteriously disappeared
near the forest, along with his entire flock

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.130
of 200 sheep.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.910
But that was only the start.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:23.790
In the 1960s a biologist named Alexandru Sift,
who was studying the forest, took a series

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:29.390
of unbelievable photos of a disc-shaped object
hovering in the sky above the forest.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:35.940
Again, in 1968, military technician, Emil
Barnea captured another infamous photo of

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.810
a flying saucer over Hoia-Baciu Forest.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:44.590
The have been numerous reports of people going
missing in the forest and many people who

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.210
visit the forest report seeing otherworldly
apparitions.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:53.250
This has led many to believe that the forest
is a portal to another dimension.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:59.479
Next up we go to Japan for another horrifically
bizarre forest, but this one has a bit more

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:01.360
of a macabre legacy.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.200
Aokigahara forest sits silently at the base
of Mt.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.200
Fuji.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.379
It may look harmless, but this one's a biter!

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:12.519
Aokigahara Forest is known locally as "Suicide
Forest".

00:02:12.519 --> 00:02:17.989
That's because every year people travel here
in their droves just to commit suicide.

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:22.510
Every year over 100 people commit suicide
in Aokigahara Forest.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.659
Most victims of the Forest's disturbing allure
hang themselves from the tree branches.

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:30.859
The worst bit is that the problem's not getting
any better.

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:33.810
Every year the number of suicides in the forest
increases.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:39.959
Annual body searches have to be conducted
by police and volunteers to seek out and remove

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:45.139
the hundreds of corpses of the unfortunate
souls that the forest has claimed.

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:51.150
Nowhere else in the world do people so habitually
commit suicide by hanging in a single location,

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.040
at least not in these disturbingly high numbers.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:59.400
This irregularity has led locals to erect
signs in the forest urging people not to kill

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.400
themselves.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.129
The signs contain words of optimism, such
as "Your life is a precious gift from your

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.260
parents" and "Think of your family".

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:13.969
No one quite knows for sure why this particular
expanse of trees is chosen as the final resting

00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:16.550
place for hundreds of people each year.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.559
What on earth compels them to choose Aokigahara
forest?

00:03:20.559 --> 00:03:25.699
Some say it's because of a 1960 novel called
Kuroi Jukai, which is about a young lover

00:03:25.699 --> 00:03:29.169
who commits suicide in Aokigahara forest.

00:03:29.169 --> 00:03:34.969
Poveglia Island in the Venetian Lagoon, Italy,
is said to be one of the most haunted places

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:36.069
on Earth.

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.379
Located only a stone's throw away from the
romantic utopia that is Venice, sits an island

00:03:41.379 --> 00:03:45.959
that is a stark contrast to the captivating
eyes of water-bound lovers.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:51.199
Poveglia Island is known as "Plauge Island",
because it was used as a quarantine station

00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:53.589
for people who had The Plague.

00:03:53.589 --> 00:04:00.540
Over 160,000 plague sufferers were sent to
this island to be isolated from society.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:06.290
About 95% of those people never left the island,
because when they died from the plague on

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:12.109
the island, which was most of them, they were
burned or buried right there on the island.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:16.910
Mass graves were made on the island and thousands
upon thousands of corpses were dumped on top

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.930
of one another and either burned or left to
rot.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:25.840
So many human remains were disposed of on
this island, that the soil is said to consist

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.510
of 50% human ashes.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.669
Perfect for growing turnips.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:33.340
So, yeah, that's disturbing, but there's more.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.990
As if this island hadn't seen enough tragedy.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:42.330
Between 1922 and 1968 there was a mental asylum
on the island.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.340
The doctor at the asylum tortured and killed
his own patients.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.330
He would also conduct horrific experiments
on them.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:53.650
Until he eventually went crazy and killed
himself by jumping out of the bell tower of

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.330
the asylum.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.590
Chapels are meant to be places for contemplation
and redemption, but not this one.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.600
Unless you prefer to say your prayers amongst
the dead.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.229
Because this chapel in Portugal is lined from
head to toe in human skeletal remains.

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:15.990
The chapel, aptly named the Chapel of Bones,
contains the bones of 5,000 monks and to top

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:22.500
it off there are two bodies hanging from ropes
inside the chapel and one is the body of a

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.500
child.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:27.659
If you happen to have a twisted fetish for
human bones you might also be interested in

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:29.300
The Sedlec Ossuary.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:33.691
Similar to the Chapel of bones, this small
chapel in the Czech Republic is covered in

00:05:33.691 --> 00:05:34.979
human bones.

00:05:34.979 --> 00:05:38.139
Seriously, why do people keep making things
out of bones?

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:39.979
I’ll tell you why.

00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:44.310
Because so many people were being buried there
that the priests ran out of space, so they

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.919
decided to decorate the chapel's interior
with their bodies.

00:05:47.919 --> 00:05:48.919
Lovely.

00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:52.430
Oh, they even made furnishings with human
bones too.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.080
Wood and nails are so overrated.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.389
Next, to Scotland.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:01.919
This creepy bridge called Overtoun Bridge
is haunted by a mysterious, unknown force,

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:04.599
that wills dogs to their death.

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:10.550
For unknown reasons hundreds of dogs have
spontaneously committed suicide on this bridge

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.509
by jumping off it.

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:17.810
Hundreds of dog owners have reported walking
their beloved pet along this 15 metre tall

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:22.960
bridge, when suddenly the dog goes crazy and
leaps off the side of the bridge without warning.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.840
The cases always happen around the same point
along the bridge.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:32.690
Over 50 dogs in the past 50 years have taken
their own life in the exact same way on Overtoun

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:33.840
Bridge.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.530
So what is causing these animals to kill themselves?

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:41.409
After all, dogs are usually rather happy little
fellas; it’s largely unheard of for a dog

00:06:41.409 --> 00:06:43.300
to take their own life.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.729
Is it an evil spirit haunting the bridge?

00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:48.580
Or does the sight of the bridge just freak
them out?

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:53.969
In Celtic mythology, Overtoun is known as
"The Thin Place", an area where heaven and

00:06:53.969 --> 00:06:56.169
earth are said to be very close.

00:06:56.169 --> 00:07:02.340
Some believe dogs are more sensitive to paranormal
forces and if Celtic mythology is correct,

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:05.889
this bridge is flooded with both good and
evil spirits.

00:07:05.889 --> 00:07:10.740
However scientists who have studied the bridge
have a more rational explanation.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.560
They found a colony of mink that reside underneath
the bridge.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.439
The mink's powerful anal glands leave scent
marks wherever they go and this smell has

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:23.320
proven to be irresistible to dogs during trials.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:28.139
So the most likely explanation is that the
dogs are uncontrollably drawn to the enticing

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:34.249
scent of musty mink anus below the bridge
and, unwise to the dangers of high places,

00:07:34.249 --> 00:07:37.620
they throw themselves off the bridge in pursuit
of the smell.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:40.560
Sadly betrayed by their own noses.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:46.860
In Columbia County, Pennsylvania is a borough
called Centralia that is a real-life ghost

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:47.860
town.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.069
In 1981 Centralia had a population of over
1,000.

00:07:52.069 --> 00:07:55.840
Today it has a population of just 10.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.969
So what happened?

00:07:56.969 --> 00:07:58.599
Where did everyone go?

00:07:58.599 --> 00:08:02.050
Centralia used to be a thriving coal mining
community.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:06.280
In 1962 a fire started in a mine beneath the
town.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.969
Which is not good considering the entire town
sits on top of a huge vein of coal.

00:08:10.969 --> 00:08:15.370
The townsfolk tried everything they could
to put the fire out including smothering it

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:21.740
with water and even covering it in clay, but
it continued to burn, regardless.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:25.810
The fire quickly spread to numerous other
mines underneath the town.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:29.960
Then the ground, all over the town, started
to collapse due to the immense heat coming

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.890
from the fire raging away below ground.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.970
Pavements started to crack and crumble.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:39.210
Houses collapsed without warning and sinkholes
appeared in random locations.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.580
Engulfing buildings and people.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:46.830
The people of Centralia decided the town was
no longer safe to live in and with no hope

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.090
of ever extinguishing the fire, everyone left.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.330
Apart from 10 stubborn people who refused
to leave.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:58.420
Most of the building have either collapsed
due to the fire, or been left abandoned for

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.210
nature to take over.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:05.400
Today Centralia is a near ghost town; the
main road which passed through the town, has

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.720
been blocked off because it's too dangerous.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.880
Signs have also been erected throughout the
town, warning people of the severe dangers

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.010
posed by the never-ending, underground fire.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:22.790
It is estimated that at its current rate the
fire will continue to burn for another 250

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:23.880
years.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:29.050
Just south of Mexico City in the middle of
a swamp-like canal sits the creepiest island

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.300
in the world.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:34.660
Named Isla de las Munecas, which translates
as Island of the Dolls.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:39.350
This terrifying place is covered in child's
dolls, and not the pretty kind either.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:44.490
Nope, this island is decorated with hundreds
of horrific, possessed dolls that totally

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.830
wouldn't hesitate to murder you in your sleep.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.630
So, the obvious question has to be asked.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.420
Why the hell would anyone do this?

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.380
Well the story goes like this.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:10:00.380
The island's caretaker and its only inhabitant,
Don Julian Santana Barrera, found a little

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:05.240
girl in the waters of the island who had drowned
under mysterious circumstances.

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:08.190
She was found with a doll floating nearby.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:12.110
Julian picked up the doll and hung it from
a nearby tree as a mark of respect for the

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.390
deceased girl.

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.510
But one creepy doll wasn't enough for Julian.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:22.160
Apparently the spirit of the little girl haunted
him and to appease the spirit he started to

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.290
hang more dolls from trees.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.250
Before long he had covered the island with
hundreds of dolls.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:32.830
Julian started to believe that all the dolls
were possessed by the spirits of dead girls

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:35.910
and this slowly drove him to insanity.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:42.100
After 50 years of collecting and hanging up
dolls, Julian was found dead in the water.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:47.450
He had mysteriously drowned in the exact same
spot where the little girl's body was supposedly

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.420
found, all those years ago.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:56.260
Some say that the little girl never actually
existed and Julian made up the story as a

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:59.400
way of coping with his isolation on the island.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.510
But no one really knows the truth.

